build-demo-warrior-name = Warrior
build-demo-warrior-description = RFB's weapon-first career with exceptional melee and shooting growth, 115% life, limited device skill, and no spellcasting; advanced career powers remain pending.
build-demo-high-mage-death-name = High-Mage · Death
build-demo-high-mage-death-description = A single-realm High-Mage specializing in Death magic, with the complete four-book progression and RFB's original High-Mage spell parameters.
build-demo-archer-name = Archer
build-demo-archer-description = An ammunition-crafting specialist with unmatched skill using bows, crossbows and slings.
build-demo-paladin-death-name = Paladin · Death
build-demo-paladin-death-description = A Death-realm Paladin who prays with Wisdom and receives new prayers as random divine gifts.
race-demo-rfb-human-name = Human
race-demo-rfb-human-description = RFB's unmodified Human profile using the Standard humanoid equipment body.
class-demo-warrior-name = Warrior
class-demo-warrior-description = A direct-combat career using RFB's original attribute, health, experience, and skill-growth values. It relies on weapons and only occasional devices.
class-demo-high-mage-name = High-Mage
class-demo-high-mage-description = High-Mages specialize in one realm and master it far beyond ordinary mages. In return for giving up a second realm, they gain substantially improved spell costs, power, level requirements and failure rates, plus the Eat Magic class power at level 25. Intelligence is their primary casting attribute.
class-demo-archer-name = Archer
class-demo-archer-description = Archers are to bows what Warriors are to melee. They are the best class with bows, crossbows and slings, and learn to make ammunition from dungeon debris. Archers are also better than Warriors at stealth, perception, searching and using magical devices.
class-demo-paladin-name = Paladin
class-demo-paladin-description = Paladins combine the strengths of Warriors and Priests. They excel in melee, but are mediocre at ranged combat, stealth, perception, and magical devices; their divine alliance grants a good saving throw. Wisdom governs their prayers. Paladins choose one realm from Life, Crusade, Daemon, and Death, and receive new prayers as divine gifts rather than choosing them. They can learn every prayer, though more slowly than Priests, and can gain experience by destroying advanced heretical spellbooks. Their realm alignment determines whether their class power is Holy Lance or Hell Lance.
ability-demo-paladin-hell-lance-name = Hell Lance
ability-demo-paladin-hell-lance-description = Fires a beam of pure hellfire.
personality-demo-ordinary-name = Ordinary
personality-demo-ordinary-description = A neutral personality with no additional modifiers.
personality-demo-combat-name = Combat
personality-demo-combat-description = Trades some technical aptitude for direct combat skill.
skill-demo-disarming-name = Disarming
skill-demo-disarming-description = Aptitude for locks, traps, and mechanisms.
skill-demo-device-name = Devices
skill-demo-device-description = Aptitude for magical and mechanical devices.
skill-demo-saving-throw-name = Saving Throw
skill-demo-saving-throw-description = Aptitude for resisting hostile effects and abilities.
skill-demo-stealth-name = Stealth
skill-demo-stealth-description = Aptitude for avoiding enemy notice.
skill-demo-search-name = Search
skill-demo-search-description = Aptitude for actively finding concealed terrain and mechanisms.
skill-demo-perception-name = Perception
skill-demo-perception-description = Aptitude for passively noticing unusual details.
skill-demo-melee-name = Melee
skill-demo-melee-description = Aptitude for landing ordinary close-combat attacks.
skill-demo-ranged-name = Shooting
skill-demo-ranged-description = Aptitude for hitting distant targets with launchers.
skill-demo-throwing-name = Throwing
skill-demo-throwing-description = Aptitude for hitting targets with thrown items.
skill-demo-digging-name = Digging
skill-demo-digging-description = Aptitude for clearing destructible terrain.

